$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["1.3"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 1.3. The median number of tourists is found by ordering the number of tourists from least to greatest and determining the middle value from this list. When the number of tourists in 2012 is ordered from least to greatest, the middle value, or the fifth number, is 46.4 million. When the number of tourists in 2013 is ordered from least to greatest, the middle value, or the fifth number, is 47.7 million. The difference between these two medians is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/07f2829b/img_000_2c28a132.png" alt="47 point 7 million minus 46 point 4 million, equals 1 point 3 million"></span>. Note that 1.3 and 13/10 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
