$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The frequency distribution above summarizes a set of data, where <em class="inline_variable ">a</em> is a positive integer. How much greater is the mean of the set of data than the median?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. Since the frequencies of values less than the middle value, 3, are the same as the frequencies of the values greater than 3, the set of data has a symmetric distribution. When a set of data has a symmetric distribution, the mean and median values are equal. Therefore, the mean is 0 greater than the median.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from misinterpreting the set of data.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
