erTd td7c51c75f-c815-4437-8ef3-5e508c3b3782\"><span class=\"italic \">a</span></td>\n\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t</tbody>\n\t\t</table>\n\t</div>\n</div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The frequency distribution above summarizes a set of data, where <em class=\"inline_variable \">a</em> is a positive integer. How much greater is the mean of the set of data than the median?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Since the frequencies of values less than the middle value, 3, are the same as the frequencies of the values greater than 3, the set of data has a symmetric distribution. When a set of data has a symmetric distribution, the mean and median values are equal. Therefore, the mean is 0 greater than the median.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from misinterpreting the set of data.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959626,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"1142af44","skill_cd":"Q.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","createDate":1691007959626,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"029610-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"4fb4123a-301e-4e0b-a0f2-c268476fd9ba","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"029610-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\">\n\t<div>\n\t\t<table class=\"tableWithBorder\" style=\"width:100px;\">\n\t\t\t<tbody>\n\t\t\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"tableWithBorderTd td4869ff00-136c-40bd-9105-94932f1fce3a\">Value</td>