requencies of the values greater than 3, the set of data has a symmetric distribution. When a set of data has a symmetric distribution, the mean and median values are equal. Therefore, the mean is 0 greater than the median.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from misinterpreting the set of data.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959626,"updateDate":1691007959626}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959626, 1691007959626),
    ($SATQ$1180401d$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$10619-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The total area of a coastal city is 92.1&nbsp;square miles, of which 11.3&nbsp;square miles is water. If the city had a population of 621,000&nbsp;people in the year 2010, which of the following is closest to the population density, in people per square mile of land area, of the city at that&nbsp;time?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"phantom_text \"><p>6,740</p></span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"phantom_text \"><p>7,690</p></span>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>55,000</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>76,000</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The land area of the coastal city can be found by subtracting the area of the water from the total area of the coastal city; that is, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1180401d/img_000_49244d90.png" alt="92 point 1, minus 11 point 3, equals 80 point 8"></span> square miles. The population density is the population divided by the land area, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1180401d/img_001_bb66fa0e.png" alt="the fraction 621,000 over 80 point 8, end fraction, equals 7,686"></span>, which is closest to 7,690 people per square mile.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may be the result of dividing the population by the total area, instead of the land area. Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of dividing the population by the area of water. Choice D is incorrect and may be the result of making a computational error with the decimal place.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"1180401d","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"10619-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The total area of a coastal city is 92.1&nbsp;square miles, of which 11.3&nbsp;square miles is water. If the city had a population of 621,000&nbsp;people in the year 2010, which of the following is closest to the population density, in people per square mile of land area, of the city at that&nbsp;time?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"phantom_text \"><p>6,740</p></span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"phantom_text \"><p>7,690</p></span>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>55,000</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>76,000</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The land area of the coastal city can be found by subtracting the area of the water from the total area of the coastal city; that is, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1180401d/img_000_49244d90.png\" alt=\"92 point 1, minus 11 point 3, equals 80 point 8\"></span> square miles. The population density is the population divided by the land area, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1180401d/img_001_bb66fa0e.png\" alt=\"the fraction 621,000 over 80 point 8, end fraction, equals 7,686\"></span>, which is closest to 7,690 people per square mile.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may be the result of dividing the population by the total area, instead of the land area. Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of dividing the population by the area of water. Choice D is incorrect and may be the result of making a computational error with the decimal place.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":2,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959638,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"1180401d","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1691007959638,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"10619-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"b62ee979-5612-4564-a90b-e17977f2b6bf","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"10619-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The total area of a coastal city is 92.1&nbsp;square miles, of which 11.3&nbsp;square miles is water. If the city had a population of 621,000&nbsp;people in the year 2010, which of the following is closest to the population density, in people per square mile of land area, of the city at that&nbsp;time?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<span class=\"phantom_text \"><p>6,740</p></span>\n"},"b":{"body":"<span class=\"phantom_text \"><p>7,690</p></span>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>55,000</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>76,000</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The land area of the coastal city can be found by subtracting the area of the water from the total area of the coastal city; that is, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"92 point 1, minus 11 point 3, equals 80 point 8\"></span> square miles. The population density is the population divided by the land area, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 621,000 over 80 point 8, end fraction, equals 7,686\"></span>, which is closest to 7,690 people per square mile.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may be the result of dividing the population by the total area, instead of the land area. Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of dividing the population by the area of water. Choice D is incorrect and may be the result of making a computational error with the decimal place.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959638,"updateDate":1691007959638}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959638, 1691007959638),
    ($SATQ$11b06e35$SATQ$, $SATQ$d6f5d386-dd70-4e85-96cc-2c0859c39acc$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The density of a certain solid substance is <math alttext="813"><mn>813</mn>
</math><cite>&nbsp;</cite>kilograms per cubic meter. A sample of this substance is in the shape of a cube, where each edge has a length of <math alttext="0.60"><mn>0.60</mn></math><cite>&nbsp;</cite>meters. To the nearest whole number, what is the mass, in kilograms, of this sample?&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2d597fb7-fd3a-451c-b6d1-9e9453b12348","content":"<p><math alttext=\"176\"><mn>176</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"905da05c-d10f-4051-b3e4-66c7feb1fd8d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"488\"><mn>488</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b1bf11c2-42ba-4958-8707-a955fa078e9f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,355\"><mn>1,355</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d140d532-420b-4925-9a9a-32dc4eca3e70","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3,764\"><mn>3,764</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2d597fb7-fd3a-451c-b6d1-9e9453b12348"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that the sample is in the shape of a cube with edge lengths of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0.60"><mn>0.60</mn></math> meters. Therefore, the volume of the sample is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0.60 cubed"><msup><mn>0.60</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0.216"><mn>0.216</mn></math>, cubic meters. It's also given that the sample has a density of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="813"><mn>813</mn></math> kilograms per <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> cubic meter. Therefore, the mass of this sample is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0.216 cubic meters right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 813 kilograms Over 1 cubic meter EndFraction right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0.216</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>cubic</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>meters</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>813</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kilograms</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>cubic</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>meter</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="175.608"><mn>175.608</mn></math> kilograms. Rounding this mass to the nearest whole number gives <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="176"><mn>176</mn></math> kilograms. Therefore, to the nearest whole number, the mass, in kilograms, of this sample is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="176"><mn>176</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"11b06e35","external_id":"d6f5d386-dd70-4e85-96cc-2c0859c39acc","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"ef368fb9-1846-418b-8940-513269e156cd","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The density of a certain solid substance is <math alttext=\"813\"><mn>813</mn>\n</math><cite>&nbsp;</cite>kilograms per cubic meter. A sample of this substance is in the shape of a cube, where each edge has a length of <math alttext=\"0.60\"><mn>0.60</mn></math><cite>&nbsp;</cite>meters. To the nearest whole number, what is the mass, in kilograms, of this sample?&nbsp;</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2d597fb7-fd3a-451c-b6d1-9e9453b12348","content":"<p><math alttext=\"176\"><mn>176</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"905da05c-d10f-4051-b3e4-66c7feb1fd8d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"488\"><mn>488</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b1bf11c2-42ba-4958-8707-a955fa078e9f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,355\"><mn>1,355</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d140d532-420b-4925-9a9a-32dc4eca3e70","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3,764\"><mn>3,764</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["2d597fb7-fd3a-451c-b6d1-9e9453b12348"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that the sample is in the shape of a cube with edge lengths of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0.60\"><mn>0.60</mn></math> meters. Therefore, the volume of the sample is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0.60 cubed\"><msup><mn>0.60</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"ht