    ($SATQ$121dc44f$SATQ$, $SATQ$db08d5bc-9768-4b87-8642-1033890325ea$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$08dd548c-5c15-49e4-9094-90ad0daa3346$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The population of City A increased by <math alttext="7 percent sign"><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> from <math alttext="2015"><mn>2015</mn></math> to <math alttext="2016"><mn>2016</mn></math>. If the <math alttext="2016"><mn>2016</mn></math> population is <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> times the <math alttext="2015"><mn>2015</mn></math> population, what is the value of <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f8bcb593-072d-4b94-acf6-f7b65d64ab84","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.07\"><mrow><mn>0.07</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"31d148a8-4ad9-40d4-83ab-e10dfed1be7f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.7\"><mrow><mn>0.7</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"e7427371-93d6-4f75-918e-93afbeab6df6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1.07\"><mrow><mn>1.07</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"0b7e858e-35dc-43ce-ab9c-a2cae1903fbf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1.7\"><mrow><mn>1.7</mn></mrow></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e7427371-93d6-4f75-918e-93afbeab6df6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It's given that the population of City A increased by <math alttext="7 percent sign"><mn>7</mn><mo>%</mo></math> from <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="20 16"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>16</mn>
</math>. Therefore, the population of City A in <math alttext="20 16"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>16</mn>
</math> includes <math alttext="100 percent sign"><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the population of City A in <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math> plus an additional <math alttext="7 percent sign"><mn>7</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the population of City A in <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math>. This means that the population of City A in <math alttext="20 16"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>16</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="107 percent sign"><mn>107</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the population in <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math>. Thus, the population of City A in <math alttext="20 16"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>16</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="StartFraction 107 Over 100 EndFraction"><mfrac>
	<mn>107</mn>
	<mn>100</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>, or <math alttext="1.07"><mn>1.07</mn>
</math>, times the <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math> population. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="1.07"><mn>1.07</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This would be the value of <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> if the population in <math alttext="20 16"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>16</mn>
</math> was <math alttext="7 percent sign"><mn>7</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the population in <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This would be the value of <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> if the population in <math alttext="20 16"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>16</mn>
</math> was <math alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the population in <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This would be the value of <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> if the population increased by <math alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, not <math alttext="7 percent sign"><mn>7</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, from <math alttext="20 15"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>15</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="20 16"><mn>20</mn>
<mn>16</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"121dc44f","external_id":"db08d5bc-9768-4b87-8642-1033890325ea","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"08dd548c-5c15-49e4-9094-90ad0daa3346","uId":"52b4a07f-657d-4b2b-b9e8-cde51e3f2aad","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>The population of City A increased by <math alttext=\"7 percent sign\"><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> from <math alttext=\"2015\"><mn>2015</mn></math> to <math alttext=\"2016\"><mn>2016</mn></math>. If the <math alttext=\"2016\"><mn>2016</mn></math> population is <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> times the <math alttext=\"2015\"><mn>2015</mn></math> population, what is the value of <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f8bcb593-072d-4b94-acf6-f7b65d64ab84","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.07\"><mrow><mn>0.07</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"31d148a8-4ad9-40d4-83ab-e10dfed1be7f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.7\"><mrow><mn>0.7</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"e7427371-93d6-4f75-918e-93afbeab6df6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1.07\"><mrow><mn>1.07</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"0b7e858e-35dc-43ce-ab9c-a2cae1903fbf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1.7\"><mrow><mn>1.7</mn></mrow></math></p>"}],"keys":["e7427371-93d6-4f75-918e-93afbeab6df6"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It's given that the population of City A increased by <math alttext=\"7 percent sign\"><mn>7</mn><mo>%</mo></math> from <math alttext=\"20 15\"><mn>20</mn>\n<mn>15</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"20 16\"><mn>20</mn>\n<mn>16</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, the population of City A in <math alttext=\"20 16\"><mn>20</mn>\n<mn>16</mn>\n</math> includes <math a