=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the maximum, not the mean, of the data shown.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"32\"><mn>32</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p>What is the mean of the data shown?</p>","externalid":"43a2c649-5ad6-4d16-9779-da333ff1569a","templateid":"72e68e29-0e89-4d17-b2fe-d3f34aaac1c5","vaultid":"ccf9103c-78ed-4b6a-936a-c1bfe212ac48","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"6b849fb1-cd2c-41ec-986b-8b590f24bea9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"daccd943-3511-4be5-919b-0fa9e258cb39","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ff6439df-12b4-4d05-9aa4-40d43d7ec349","content":"<p><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1ece136c-445d-4707-8627-f597eec1f6c8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"32\"><mn>32</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959833,"updateDate":1691007959833}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959833, 1691007959833),
    ($SATQ$12dbe3de$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$022066-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">A store received a shipment of 1,000&nbsp;MP3 players, 4&nbsp;of which were defective. If an MP3 player is randomly selected from this shipment, what is the probability that it is defective?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0.004</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0.04</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0.4</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. The probability of randomly selecting a defective MP3 player from the shipment is equal to the number of defective MP3 players divided by the total number of MP3 players in the shipment. Therefore, the probability is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/12dbe3de/img_000_ac3e9a93.png" alt="4 over 1,000"></span>, which is equivalent to 0.004.<p>Choice B is incorrect because 0.04 represents 4 defective MP3 players out of 100 rather than out of 1,000. Choice C is incorrect because 0.4 represents 4 defective MP3 players out of 10 rather than out of 1,000. Choice D is incorrect. This is the number of defective MP3 players in the shipment.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
