nt-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Probability of snow (%)</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="89.83634185791016" y1="48" x2="89.83634185791016" y2="248" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"></line><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="124.23179912567139" x2="124.23179912567139" y1="48" y2="248" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"></line><text xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="end" transform="translate(134.15179912567137 267.84) rotate(-40)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Tuesday</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="193.02271366119385" x2="193.02271366119385" y1="48" y2="248" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"></line><text xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="end" transform="translate(202.94271366119384 267.84) rotate(-40)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Wednesday</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="261.8136281967163" x2="261.8136281967163" y1="48" y2="248" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"></line><text xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="end" transform="translate(271.7336281967163 267.84) rotate(-40)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Thursday</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="330.60454273223877" x2="330.60454273223877" y1="48" y2="248" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"></line><text xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="end" transform="translate(340.5245427322388 267.84) rotate(-40)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Friday</text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(227.41817092895508 24)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text"></text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(227.41817092895508 357.6453283691406)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Day of the week</text><line x1="124.23179912567139" y1="128" x2="193.02271366119385" y2="68" stroke="#000" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#marker0)" marker-start="url(#marker0)"></line><line x1="193.02271366119385" y1="68" x2="261.8136281967163" y2="188" stroke="#000" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#marker0)" marker-start="url(#marker0)"></line><line x1="261.8136281967163" y1="188" x2="330.60454273223877" y2="108" stroke="#000" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#marker0)" marker-start="url(#marker0)"></line></g></svg><div role="region" aria-label="Long description for line graph" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>The line graph:<br>
<ul>
<li>Begins at Tuesday, 60%</li>
<li>Rises sharply to Wednesday, 90%</li>
<li>Falls sharply to Thursday, 30%</li>
<li>Rises sharply to Friday, 70%</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The line graph shows the probability of snow, as a percent, at a certain location for each day during a four-day period. According to the line graph, for which day during this four-day period is the probability of snow <math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b5c0bf27-c965-4678-8165-b282c884d92c","content":"<p>Tuesday</p>"},{"id":"5e8ba769-09f9-4146-88f8-009bd0530c16","content":"<p>Wednesday</p>"},{"id":"d5b995ff-6518-4bab-a0c3-9ba4af88e450","content":"<p>Thursday</p>"},{"id":"1d6bd374-d17a-4046-ada7-a9dabb0daaed","content":"<p>Friday</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d5b995ff-6518-4bab-a0c3-9ba4af88e450"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. For the line graph shown, the probability of snow, as a percent, is represented on the vertical axis. According to the line graph, during this four-day period, the probability of snow is&nbsp;<math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> for Thursday.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. The probability of snow on Tuesday is <math alttext="60 percent sign"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The probability of snow on Wednesday is <math alttext="90 percent sign"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. The probability of snow on Friday is <math alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"13f67ddc","external_id":"76bc1af1-9e88-4760-961f-db2050ad9091","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"58c10e05-aec7-4e7d-9d53-0fcbc24a23ea","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"380\" height=\"385.8053283691406\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 385.8053283691406\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A line graph. The horizontal axis is labeled Day of the week. It ranges from Tuesday to Friday in increments of 1 day. The vertical axis is labeled Probability of snow, in percent. It ranges from 0 to 100 in increments of 10. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"ed420550-79eb-48d4-af01-cd27cdd08afd\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><defs>\n      <marker id=\"marker0\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" refX=\"3\" refY=\"3\" markerUnits=\"strokeWidth\">\n        <circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"3\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\".6\"></circle>\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"marker1\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" refX=\"3\" refY=\"3\" markerUnits=\"strokeWidth\">\n        <circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"3\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#FFF\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\".6\"></circle>\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"marker2\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" refX=\"2.5\" refY=\"2.5\" markerUnits=\"strokeWidth\">\n        <polygon points=\"2.37 0, -0.02 4.12, 4.73 4.12\" fill=\"#000\"></polygon>\n      </marker>\n      <marker id=\"marker3\" markerWidth=\"3.75\" markerHeight=\"3.75\" refX=\"2\" 