n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The line graph shows the probability of snow, as a percent, at a certain location for each day during a four-day period. According to the line graph, for which day during this four-day period is the probability of snow <math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b5c0bf27-c965-4678-8165-b282c884d92c","content":"<p>Tuesday</p>"},{"id":"5e8ba769-09f9-4146-88f8-009bd0530c16","content":"<p>Wednesday</p>"},{"id":"d5b995ff-6518-4bab-a0c3-9ba4af88e450","content":"<p>Thursday</p>"},{"id":"1d6bd374-d17a-4046-ada7-a9dabb0daaed","content":"<p>Friday</p>"}],"keys":["d5b995ff-6518-4bab-a0c3-9ba4af88e450"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. For the line graph shown, the probability of snow, as a percent, is represented on the vertical axis. According to the line graph, during this four-day period, the probability of snow is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> for Thursday.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. The probability of snow on Tuesday is <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. The probability of snow on Wednesday is <math alttext=\"90 percent sign\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. The probability of snow on Friday is <math alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357405,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"13f67ddc","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1730147357405,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_