.992027 \nL 234.421913 69.978795 \nL 237.25874 57.718774 \nL 240.095567 44.582444 \nL 242.121872 34.628315 \nL 242.121872 34.628315 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"pe48e1e503d\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"276.113284\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for Answer Choice D\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>The scatterplot has 8 data points.</li>\n<li>The data points are in an exponential pattern trending up from left to right.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>A curve of best fit is shown:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The curve of best fit trends up from left to right.</li>\n<li>2 points are touching the curve of best fit.</li>\n<li>3 points are above the curve of best fit.</li>\n<li>3 points are below the curve of best fit.</li>\n<li>The curve of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 51)</li>\n<li>(4 comma 851)</li>\n<li>(6 comma 3,472)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["86ed8ec0-601e-4024-8e5e-ad8ebb6eb778"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. An appropriate model should follow the trend of the data points and should have data points both above and below the model. The scatterplot shows that the data points have an increasing trend that is curved. Therefore, an appropriate model should be an increasing curve with data points both above and below the model. Of the given choices, only the model in choice D is an increasing curve with data points both above and below the model.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. Since the trend of the data points isn't linear, a line isn't the most appropriate model for the data.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. Since the trend of the data points is increasing and isn't linear, a decreasing line isn't the most appropriate model for the data.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. All the data points are below the model shown in this graph.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"15ce8207","external_id":"aee1cc54-9f2e-46de-94fa-2cccbe708d41","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"1e8f80bc-5808-4025-8ac3-14ee5e0e3e50","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 291.371642 275.22\" width=\"291.371642pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 7. The y axis ranges from 0 to 5,000. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 291.371642 275.22 \nL 291.371642 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 12.011642 260.46 \nL 284.171642 260.46 \nL 284.171642 10.98 \nL 12.011642 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 268.02 \nL 283.313284 268.02 \nL 283.313284 7.2 \nL 7.2 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_3\">\n    <g id=\"xtic