<p style="text-align: left;">How many more students are in drama than in chess?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d5215053-6b52-4040-956c-0c7af06af29d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"06736a5e-3f45-474a-aef6-23edc04d133b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"30\"><mn>30</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"69304518-d087-4204-b072-3c3776da146e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5502a2a2-aad3-4eff-a89a-3a8471fbe4c0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d5215053-6b52-4040-956c-0c7af06af29d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that the bar graph shows the distribution of the number of students in each of four extracurricular activities at a high school. The bar representing drama has a height of <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math>; therefore, there are <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math> students in drama. The bar representing chess has a height of <math alttext="30"><mn>30</mn>
</math>; therefore, there are <math alttext="30"><mn>30</mn>
</math> students in chess. Thus, there are <math alttext="40 minus 30"><mn>40</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></math>, or <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> more students in drama than in chess.</p>
